# Ticket #4471 — Calendar and booking date discrepancies

Ticket #4471 merged 412 unique reports about calendar invites and booking dates not matching. Analysis found two distinct root causes, both stemming from locale handling failures.

## Problems identified

| Cause | Count | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| Parser reads dates month-first; tenants write day-first | 379 | The shared parser reads every date month first. When a day-first tenant uses app, email, or form channels, their dates are flipped: 4 July becomes 7 April, 10 March becomes 3 October. Affects users in day-first locales across all channels. |
| Form hint says MM/DD but tenant types DD/MM | 33 | Through booking-v3, day-first tenants see a MM/DD/YYYY hint but type DD/MM (their locale). The form reads their input the same way, creating the same inversion. Specific to booking-v3 users in day-first locales. |

**Total: 412 unique reports across 2 categories**

## Root cause analysis

Both issues stem from the system's assumption that dates are month-first, conflicting with day-first locales. The parser bug dominates (379 reports, 92% of merged reports), affecting all channels (app, email, form) and day-first locales including en-GB, nl-NL, cs-CZ, de-DE, it-IT, da-DK, pt-PT, pl-PL, fr-FR, es-ES, and en-IE. The form hint issue is smaller (33 reports, 8% of merged reports) but stems from the same root cause: booking-v3 shows MM/DD but day-first tenants type DD/MM.

## Next steps

Each problem type has been filed as a separate issue in the GitHub repo so the engineering team can investigate and fix them independently.

